findings.recommendation:
Out of scope for Task 03's diff - do not widen this task. Register as tech debt next to [020]/[021] and fix in the stat layer:

  func (r *PGresult) sort(key int, desc bool) {
      if r.Nrows == 0 || key < 0 {
          return
      }
      for i := range r.Values {
          if key >= len(r.Values[i]) {
              return /* key outside the result: leave input order */
          }
      }
      ...

Alternatively (or additionally) clamp in report/report.go before countDiff: if `v.OrderKey >= len(d.res.Cols)` fall back to 0. Note the same guard is missing on the top/ side, where OrderKey comes from live query results and is therefore not attacker-controlled.

Not a blocker for Task 03 - the guard itself is correct and mandated by the spec; changing processData's error protocol is a separate change. When it is addressed, drain before returning, e.g. wrap the error exits in a helper:

  fail := func(err error) error {
      go func() { for { select { case <-dataCh: case <-doneCh: return } } }()
      return err
  }

or give readTar a `select { case dataCh <- d: case <-quitCh: return nil }` so the reader can be unblocked. Fixing it for the guard alone would be incomplete - all error paths share it.
